Dear all,
Have a look at our upcoming online course Invasion Genomics in R, taking place on 12, 14 and 16 October.
 
The course is designed to be asynchronous and self-paced, so you can work through the lectures and practical exercises when it suits you. On each course day, recorded lectures and self-guided tutorials with annotated R scripts will be released.
 
Although the course is self-paced, the instructor will be available throughout the course to answer questions, provide guidance and help with any problems you may encounter during the practicals. This also makes the course suitable for participants joining from different time zones.
 
The course will cover three main topics:
Movement dynamics ? invasion sources, dispersal pathways and population structure
Adaptation dynamics ? selection and adaptation in the invaded range
Genotype-by-environment associations (GEA) ? the relationship between environmental conditions and adaptation
 
